config NET_DYNTHREAD
	tristate "Dynamic threaded NAPI scheduler"
	depends on m && ARM64
	default m
	help
	  Monitor the scheduling behaviour of a target application and,
	  when it is interrupted too often by network processing, switch
	  the NAPI processing of the configured net devices from softirq
	  context to dedicated kernel threads, whose CPU affinity is
	  adapted dynamically.

	  This module can only be built as a loadable module.
